Audit: Core, AgentControl, protocol, Operation ledger, execution relation,
lease/revision/CAS, reconnect, capability discovery, wire safety, and provider
neutrality are stable and evidenced by active tests.

Decision: External Agent Protocol is frozen as the formal control contract.
JSONL stdin/stdout remains development/local transport. HTTP is deferred
candidate for remote deployment. WebSocket, CLI, and MCP are deferred; MCP is
an optional adapter and may only call the External Agent Protocol.

LLM black-box boundary: forgetting or duplicating a tool call cannot define
Core correctness; durable Operation identity and idempotency remain authority.

Real Claude JSONL: BLOCKED / ENVIRONMENT, HTTP 403 provider quota exhausted.
No provider retry performed and no missing result fabricated.

